specs\_codex-impl-delivery-live-card-2026-05-19.log:2360:packages/opencorvus/src\prompt\core\build-core.txt:114:- Never inline base64-encoded binary assets into emitted source code or artifacts. Staged attachments live at `<worktree>/references/<filename>`; reference them by relative path (`<img src="references/foo.png">`, `<image href="references/foo.png">`, `./references/foo.png` for file reads, etc.) and copy them into the deliverable's asset directory through a real file step when the runtime layout demands it. `data:<mime>;base64,...` URLs, hex-encoded blobs, or PowerShell `$bytes = [Convert]::FromBase64String(...)` heredocs embedded in generated SVG/HTML/JSON/scripts are forbidden in every form — the session write-path rejects these payloads via `InlineBase64InPartError` and downstream verification will follow.
